<html>
	<head>
		<title>Fruits</title>
		<style>
			body{
					background-color:#f9ffe6;
				}
			h1{
				text-align: center;
				color: #d32f2f;
				font-style: oblique; 
				}
			p{
				color: darkgreen;
				font-size: 18px;
				font-style:italic;
				font-family: 'Segoe UI', Tahoma, Geneva, Verdana, sans-serif;
				line-height: 1.6; 
				padding: 12;
				}
			#li1{
				color:red;
				}
			#li2{
				color:orange;
				}
			#li3{
				color:lime;
				}
			#li4{
				color:purple;
				}
				
			table{
				border-collapse: collapse;
				width: 30%;
				}
			th, td {
				border: 1px solid #ddd;
				padding: 8px;
				text-align: left;
				}
			th {
				background-color: purple;
				color: white;
				}
			tr:nth-child(even) {
				background-color: #f2f2f2;
				}
			#tr1:hover {
				background-color: #F4BB44;
				}
			#tr2:hover {
				background-color: #7B3F00 ;
				}
			#tr3:hover {
				background-color: #8fbc8f;
				}
			#tr4:hover {
				background-color: red;
				}
		</style>
	</head>
	<body>
		<h1>FRUITS</h1>
		<br>
		<p>
			Fruits are nature’s sweet and nutritious gifts, packed with vitamins, minerals, and fiber that help keep our bodies healthy.<br>
			They come in a wide variety of colors, flavors, and textures—from the juicy sweetness of mangoes and oranges to the crisp freshness of apples and pears.<br>
			Eating a variety of fruits every day can boost the immune system, improve digestion, and provide natural energy.<br>
			Whether enjoyed fresh, blended into smoothies, or added to salads and desserts, fruits are an essential part of a balanced diet and a delicious way to stay healthy.
		</p>
		
		<ul>
			<li id="li1">APPLE</li>
			<li id="li2">ORANGE</li>
			<li id="li3">BANANA</li>
			<li id="li4">grapes</li>
			etc...
		</ul>
		
		<table>
			<thead>
				<tr>
					<th>No:</th>
					<th>Name</th>
					<th>Colour</th>
					
				</tr>
			</thead>
			<tbody>
				<tr id="tr1">
					<td>1</td>
					<td>Mango</td>
					<td>Yellow</td>
				</tr>
				<tr id="tr2">
					<td>2</td>
					<td>chicku</td>
					<td>Brown</td>
				</tr>
				<tr id="tr3">
					<td>3</td>
					<td>jackfruit</td>
					<td>Green</td>
				</tr>
				<tr id="tr4">
					<td>4</td>
					<td>Strawbarry</td>
					<td>Red</td>
				</tr>
			</tbody>
		</table>
			
	</body>
</html>	
		
		